 /5V_NB nets feeding VREF-setting resistors R24\u2013R29), i.e. a per-driver reference rail, not a shared supply.\"}], \"impact\": \"The NB driver's current-reference input is shorted to the chopped motor coil output. The VREF voltage is corrupted by the coil switching, so the pump-motor current limit is wrong or unstable, and the B- output is loaded by the divider. The NB dosing pump may run at the wrong current, overheat, or fail to drive correctly.\", \"confidence\": 0.85}], \"summary\": \"The NB TMC2209's VREF pin (U7.17) and the VREF divider midpoint are tied to the motor coil output net /B_{NB}-, unlike the NA and pH channels, which have separate VREF nodes. This bridges a reference node to a switching output and is the most likely deviation from the intended design.\"}",
